      "content": "That makes sense. It's tricky because the line between \"cultural expression\" and \"toxic slang\" is so thin. \n\nLet's try a few more to see if we can find where that line is for you. I'll give you a mix of different styles. \n\nPost 5: \"I don't hate anyone, but I just feel like certain ethnic groups have a natural tendency toward higher aggression. It's just a biological observation.\"\n\nPost 6: \"Yo, chill out with all that noise, you're doing too much for no reason lol\"\n\nPost 7: \"The influx of these immigrants is going to fundamentally erode our traditional way of life and values if we don't act now.\"\n\nPost 8: \"Mr. Jones is a highly competent professional who always brings a level of sophistication to the boardroom.\"\n\nHow would you rate these? I'm curious to see how you handle the difference between 'biological' claims and 'cultural' claims, and how you treat the casual slang vs the more formal language.",
